Archwarder's [[Amulet]] was given to [[Rassimov]] by [[the Professor]] ahead of his plan to attack [[Dante Vale's house]]. Rassimov then invoked him during the battle between [[the Professor]], Dante, and [[Lok Lambert]], in order to disrupt [[Tao]] and [[Behemoth]], making them impossible to invoke. {{Source|The Secret of Two Generations}} When the team raided [[the Professor's castle]], Rassimov pretended to lose in combat against [[Dante Vale]] so that the [[Amulet]] of Archwarder could be picked up by Dante. {{source|The Divine Comedy}}

In line with Rassimov's intentions, Archwarder was then used by Dante against [[Overlos]] to allow the Puppeteer ability of [[Dendras]] to overpower the Professor's control of the Titan of Immortality. These actions led to the defeat of the Professor as well as a weakening in the influence and power of [[the Organization]]. {{source|The Mission}}

During a later battle in [[Klaus' laboratory]] upon the discovery of the Amulet of the [[Nullifier]], [[Void]], Dante used Archwarder to disrupt the [[Blood Spiral]] Titan [[Shakrit]]. However, the newly-returned Rassimov callously used [[Darkvoid]] to destroy Archwarder and his Amulet. {{source|The Blood Spiral}}

[[File:S1E26 Overlos Professor Amulet of Will Disruption Pulse.png|thumb|[[The Professor]] loses control of [[Overlos]] as the surge of energy hits the [[Amulet of Will]]]]
Archwarder has an attack power of 3 and a defense power of 3. {{source|LGS-094}}. His Disruption Pulse ability makes opposing [[Seekers]] lose control of high powered [[Titans]]. The more powerful the opposing Titan, the more susceptible it is to the ability. This can be manifested as an energy wave emitting in all directions, making it so when it comes into contact with the [[Amulet]] of a Titan, the Titan and its amulet to surge with energy and for the Seeker to lose its control {{Source|The Mission}}; however, the surge of energy can also be more focused and be targeted at either the Titan itself {{Source|The Blood Spiral}} or its amulet (preventing the Titan from being summoned in the first place) {{Source|The Secret of Two Generations}}, emerging either through Archwarder's hands or mouth.

